WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.220
Welcome to Module 1 of the Agentic AI Crash Course: the Evolution of AI.

2
00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:11.250
We will see how we got from networks that generate pictures to agents that act in the world.

3
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:18.961
In this module, you will trace nine milestones, from generative adversarial networks to Physical AI.

4
00:00:18.961 --> 00:00:28.490
You will see why Transformers and large language models became the core of modern agents, and how a language model generates text, one token at a time.

5
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.469
You will explore an interactive timeline.

6
00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:40.836
For each milestone, you will see its capabilities, typical applications, representative examples, and its contribution to agentic AI.

7
00:00:40.836 --> 00:00:44.170
Then you will run two Python labs on model inference.

8
00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:49.179
The key takeaway: agents are not a new kind of model.

9
00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:54.830
They are systems built around models, adding tools, memory, planning, and feedback.
